<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Bautzen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1018">1018</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-polish-war-1002-1018">German–Polish War (1002–1018)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bautzen">Bautzen</a> was signed on 30 January 1018 between Emperor Henry II and Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-i-the-brave">Bolesław I the Brave</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, ending fifteen years of intermittent war. Poland kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lusatia">Lusatia</a> and Milsko, and later that year German knights joined Bolesław's expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peace-of-bautzen.jpg" alt="Peace of Bautzen" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julian Nyča · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Budy%C5%A1in_%E2%80%93_pomnik_za_Budyski_m%C4%9Br.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
